[[:db/retract 17592186148223 :question/answer-fields 17592186147092] {:db/id 17592186148223 :question/problem "![](images/93/936d303dcc89c5c27e77fa3d7cfc8b63643284d9e203f176c9e0c5588c27e049.png)\n\nConsiderer the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y)$ where the graph of $f(y)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $y=1$ is a node.\n- $y=-2$ is a sink.\n- $y=3$ is a source." :question/worked-solution "We can classify the equilibrium solutions of an autonomous ODE ${y}^{′}=f(y)$ by examining its phase line.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *sink* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *toward* the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *source* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *away* from the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *node* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line point in the same direction.\n\nThe phase line that corresponds to the given graph is as follows:\n\n![](images/69/69e895d4091075f6d50eb9e44dc027c342d1fe7ca0269224c9b6a019ab312c77.png)\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n- Statement I is false. From the phase line, we see that $y=1$ is a source.\n\n- Statement II is true. From the phase line, we see that $y=-2$ is a sink.\n\n- Statement III is false. From the phase line, we see that $y=3$ is a sink.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d80f5512-0801-5f44-8705-04bc06235191"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d80f5512-0801-5f44-8705-04bc06235191" :answer-field/id #uuid "d80f5512-0801-5f44-8705-04bc06235191" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6a4eb0a3-0396-53b2-9786-1fe15d9dc42d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9cf91e35-e89f-544d-aac8-8bed29bb7a2b" "answer-61206ccb-548f-5100-91ee-609c064a5202" "answer-ec014581-93eb-5649-9c32-a31c943ef63c" "answer-6a4eb0a3-0396-53b2-9786-1fe15d9dc42d" "answer-69c30199-4328-5a15-bfcf-b46f5467a96f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9cf91e35-e89f-544d-aac8-8bed29bb7a2b" :answer/id #uuid "9cf91e35-e89f-544d-aac8-8bed29bb7a2b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-61206ccb-548f-5100-91ee-609c064a5202" :answer/id #uuid "61206ccb-548f-5100-91ee-609c064a5202" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ec014581-93eb-5649-9c32-a31c943ef63c" :answer/id #uuid "ec014581-93eb-5649-9c32-a31c943ef63c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6a4eb0a3-0396-53b2-9786-1fe15d9dc42d" :answer/id #uuid "6a4eb0a3-0396-53b2-9786-1fe15d9dc42d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-69c30199-4328-5a15-bfcf-b46f5467a96f" :answer/id #uuid "69c30199-4328-5a15-bfcf-b46f5467a96f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of these listed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147497 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-57d5be79-8453-52cc-b08d-ee25cf4792e4"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-57d5be79-8453-52cc-b08d-ee25cf4792e4" :question/id #uuid "57d5be79-8453-52cc-b08d-ee25cf4792e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-98812" :question/problem "A particular autonomous differential equation has the following properties:\n\n- $y=-3$ is a sink\n\n- $y=0$ is a source\n\n- $y=3$ is a sink\n\nWhich of the following could be the slope field of the differential equation?" :question/worked-solution "We can classify the equilibrium solutions of an autonomous ODE ${y}^{′}=f(y)$ by examining its phase line.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *sink* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *toward* the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *source* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *away* from the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *node* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line point in the same direction.\n\nFirst, we draw the phase line with the given information. \n\nNote that there are $3$ equilibrium points, $y=-3,$ $y=0,$ and $y=3.$\n\n- We're given that $y=-3$ is a sink. We represent this on the phase line by drawing a downward-pointing arrow just above $y=-3$ and an upward-pointing arrow just below it.\n\n- We're given that $y=0$ is a source. We represent this on the phase line by drawing an upward-pointing arrow just above $y=-2$ and a downward-pointing arrow just below it (already drawn by the above property).\n\n- We're given that $y=3$ is a sink. We represent this on the phase line by drawing a downward-pointing arrow just above $y=3$ and an upward-pointing arrow just below it (already drawn by the above property).\n\n![](images/a4/a4d0e0f44f77e0d29d6d226b058806e947b38f4784dc61ea609ac1040b73d7dd.png)\n\nOf the given options, the only slope field that correspond with this phase line is the following:\n\n![](images/b5/b5e7a0272bb45b9d83ec8864f58cf3b96cbb6399d079f23d168d8de5416a1c23.png)\n\nNote that:\n\n- The slope field is horizontal at $y=-3,$ $y=0,$ and $y=3.$\n\n- The slopes near $y=-3$ appear to converge toward this line.\n\n- The slopes near $y=0$ appear to diverge away from this line.\n\n- The slopes near $y=3$ appear to converge toward this line." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1c0eb52d-5859-5f17-a2af-047313c84ebc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1c0eb52d-5859-5f17-a2af-047313c84ebc" :answer-field/id #uuid "1c0eb52d-5859-5f17-a2af-047313c84ebc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1a8a7f75-ccd9-5462-8bb7-2c7b1be60406" :answer-field/choices ["answer-80ba1f07-d31e-5ece-ad1d-7de624148041" "answer-5bd318dd-9201-58a9-b18d-379eb2818d97" "answer-b82bf18a-7b1c-5303-9140-3233520ff812" "answer-bb6b5c8a-efde-53a2-864f-7808884654c5" "answer-1a8a7f75-ccd9-5462-8bb7-2c7b1be60406"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-80ba1f07-d31e-5ece-ad1d-7de624148041" :answer/id #uuid "80ba1f07-d31e-5ece-ad1d-7de624148041" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/3e/3ed74c49c2218d24dd5235f6a2f6df948d14a58edd6872ccef17ea0434c41c2b.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5bd318dd-9201-58a9-b18d-379eb2818d97" :answer/id #uuid "5bd318dd-9201-58a9-b18d-379eb2818d97" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/8d/8d608e5ab231af991d4c55ca863e95557faae55bf44ad0e8e99f7cd0417531f2.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b82bf18a-7b1c-5303-9140-3233520ff812" :answer/id #uuid "b82bf18a-7b1c-5303-9140-3233520ff812" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/9a/9a24e2ecc59eb8d152790c6850403f74fe9193cc9e3dd9f3d6ff6f38e494752d.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bb6b5c8a-efde-53a2-864f-7808884654c5" :answer/id #uuid "bb6b5c8a-efde-53a2-864f-7808884654c5" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/ae/ae926b04f1a8bb8c22cd72208b6416aa443e864083dbe4d8c2c737c049ead4f8.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1a8a7f75-ccd9-5462-8bb7-2c7b1be60406" :answer/id #uuid "1a8a7f75-ccd9-5462-8bb7-2c7b1be60406" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/b5/b5e7a0272bb45b9d83ec8864f58cf3b96cbb6399d079f23d168d8de5416a1c23.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-8f67b1d8-cc12-5be2-bedd-7d8ea39d1438" :activity/id #uuid "8f67b1d8-cc12-5be2-bedd-7d8ea39d1438" :activity/title "Classifying Equilibrium Solutions of First-Order ODEs" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048131 :activity/course 17592186046660 :activity/steps ["step-d28d673b-fc35-5482-abfa-3f1e7616614a" "step-4cca875a-cd23-5293-b9eb-53796fc6ca53"